  "notes": [
    "Source of truth: recordings of @modelcontextprotocol/server-everything 2026.8.31 (SDK 1.32.1) on 2026-10-18; behaviors not recorded follow the server's and SDK's source (node_modules), as listed below.",
    "From source, not recorded: cross-session removal of a gzip session resource re-registered by another session; tasks/list pages of 10 with the last task id as cursor; task expiry after ttl (300000 ms, restarted on completion); a queued clarification unanswered for 60 s falls back to 'technical (default - elicitation unavailable)'; a non-text clarification fails the task with 'TypeError: state.clarification.includes is not a function'; one notifications/tools/list_changed per capability-dependent tool at notifications/initialized.",
    "No network: gzip-file-as-resource fetches data: URLs itself, serves the recorded README for its default URL, and answers 'fetch failed' for any other http(s) URL (the real server's answer when the network fails).",
    "Roots: without an open GET stream the real server's roots/list is lost and times out after 60 s; the fake fails at once and waits the minute only when not in fast mode.",
    "Wall clock: research stages (1 s), tasks/result polling (1 s), task TTLs and the 5 s logging/update simulations run in real time even in fast mode, as clients observe them through tasks/get and the GET stream.",
    "zod error JSON for unusual client answers (beyond the recorded sampling/elicitation refusals) follows zod v4's issue shapes; URL normalization follows WHATWG for the URL shapes this server meets.",
    "Protocol versions (from source, not probed: introspection offers only the four known versions and a plan can't re-initialize): 2024-10-07 is supported (the recorded protocol-header refusal lists it), and an unsupported version is answered with the latest, 2025-11-25 (SDK server/index.js, LATEST_PROTOCOL_VERSION). FauxCall's runtime repeats the recorded protocol-header refusal verbatim (it names 1999-01-01, the version introspection sent) and does not check Accept or MCP-Protocol-Version on GET.",
    "Review probes recorded 2026-10-18 (plans review-*): a refused roots/list is answered at once without a log (000469); zod union refusals list every alternative and the content discriminator names its options (000473-000479); IPv6 and short IPv4 URLs pass z.url(), 999.1.1.1 does not (000481-000483); 'data:...; base64,' decodes (000484); a malformed _meta.progressToken is refused at the HTTP level with the not_jsonrpc refusal (000486); request issues are listed in schema order (000487-000489); an unfetched clarification times out after 60 s and is still delivered by a later tasks/result (000491-000500)."
  ]
